 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/techniques/black-box.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Prerequisite: Must have Black Box Reinforcement</em></p>\n<p>You have focused on using your technique to devastating effects and have learned offensive applications of your cursed technique:<br />\n<strong>Crushing Cube</strong>. As an action for 4 CE, you target a 30 feet tall, 10 feet wide square cylinder within 30 feet. All creatures in range must make a Strength saving throw. On a failure they take 5d10 necrotic damage and fall prone as they are crushed under a massive <em>Dark Cube</em>. On a success, they take half as much damage and are not prone.<br />\n<strong>Block Strike</strong>. As a bonus action for 2 CE, you cover your fist or other part of your body with a <em>Dark Cube</em> for 1 minute. You can make a melee cursed energy attack with your unarmed strikes. On a hit you deal your proficiency bonus in d4s + your CE modifier in necrotic damage.<br />\n<strong>Dark Press</strong>. As an action for 5 CE, you can create a <em>Dark Cube</em> in front of you that explodes in length on one side. All creatures in a 10 feet wide 60 feet long line must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, they take 6d8 necrotic damage and are pushed back to the edge of the line. If they impact a solid object or structure, they take the remaining distance as fall damage.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
